          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In the strict sense of the word, a
            %em cartesian product
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_2
            two
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_1\times S_2
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+pairs"} ordered pairs
            of elements in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_1
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_2
          %p
            The abstract concept of such
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            generalizes from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            to any other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            (as a special case of a category-theoretic
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            may or may not actually exist in that category.
          %p
            (If they all exist, then one speaks of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            with respect to some other
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            and on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2Cat"} 2Cat
            in contrast to the
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gray+tensor+product"} Gray tensor product
          %p
            A product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/created+limit"} created
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product"} direct product
            (for instance a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product+of+groups"} direct product of groups
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %h3#in_sets In Sets
          %p
            Given any family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_i)_{i:I}
            of sets, the
            %strong cartesian product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mi i
                  %msub
